<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Long Shot</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;With a roll of the eyes, Adora checked the ball back to her. â€œStill using the old rules?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œOf course,â€ Catra scoffed. â€œHas society fallen apart?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œSo what does winner get this time?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;With her free hand, the one that wasnâ€™t dribbling, Catra tapped her nail against her bottom lip. â€œWell, a pack of Now or Laters doesn't hold quite the same appeal it used to so... what do you want?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œIf I win, you'll come to the Elberon game?â€ Adora asked. She was trying not to light up in excitement but it was difficult. She could feel herself practically vibrating with joy. â€œI can fly you out and get you a hotel and everything.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œJust get me the ticket, dummy. I can take care of the rest. I don't need you adding one more thing to your plate.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora wanted to argue but this was already so much. She pursed her lips and nodded instead. â€œWhat do &lt;em&gt;you&lt;/em&gt; get if you win?â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œThe joy of conquering you,â€ Catra said simply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;p&gt;A visit to an old haunt. A run-in with a familiar face. A quick round of the game that brought them together.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>petty_labelle</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Explicit</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora/Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Scorpia (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Double Trouble (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Lesbian Disaster Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Lesbian Disaster Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora in a Suit (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Alternate Universe - Modern Setting</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Fluff and Smut</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Basketball</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>particularly basketball written by a person who doesn't actually like basketball</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>so you know it's good</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Gay Bar</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>play party (briefly)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>basketball star adora</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>reporter catra</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>A Tale as Old as Time</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>One Shot</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Mutual Pining</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>F/F</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>No Archive Warnings Apply</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>upon reflection by 'it's good' i mean the basketball part is short and full of inaccuracies</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>SPOP Creative Flex (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Bag>
